-- ============================================================================
-- EC3 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Probabilistic Economics, advanced tier. COMPLETES THE
-- EC3 LADDER.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: ONE CONVENTION AND WHAT TO DISTRUST. One meaning of a
-- P-label (probability of exceedance of an outcome where more is better, per
-- the Suite convention in lib/conventions/percentile.js); the NPV Scenario
-- Builder's Monte Carlo (uniform draws around the base, what each range
-- scales, the seed and what it guarantees, twenty histogram bins, the
-- S-curve downsample); two percentile rules in one module; the repaired edges
-- and one still open; and numbers to distrust.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The engine keys p10, p50 and p90 are plain
-- percentiles, so the Low case P90 of an NPV reads the p10 key. The results
-- panel that shipped before EC3-0 printed the p90 key under "P90
-- (Conservative)", so the card called conservative held the larger number.
-- A seed buys reproducibility and nothing else: medians across seeds wander
-- by more than the difference a reader is tempted to rank on.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACTS THIS TIER OWNS, every one repaired or recorded in EC3-0.
-- runMonteCarlo is seeded, no longer throws when every range is zero, and no
-- longer returns an empty S-curve below fifty iterations. The screening IRR
-- still reports its 1000 percent Newton clamp as an answer (S1), including
-- on a project that never pays back, and payback is not revisited when the
-- cumulative crosses back below zero. A tornado bar whose side cannot break
-- even collapses to zero and sorts last (B1).
--
-- The capstone grades the convention mapping, the two percentile rules and
-- the seed directly, so a reader who never learned them cannot pass it.
-- ============================================================================

